<title>USA: U.S. Easter gasoline price highest in 16 yrs - study.</title>
<headline>U.S. Easter gasoline price highest in 16 yrs - study.</headline>
<dateline>ORLANDO, Fla 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. gasoline prices are the highest for sixteen years heading into the Easter holiday, according to a study from the American Automobile Association.</p>
<p>The association's monthly report shows the average price of self-serve regular unleaded gasoline is $1.271 per gallon, 9.1 cents more than one year ago and the highest for Easter since 1981 when the price reached $1.388.</p>
<p>The Association noted that the price for gasoline had dropped by 1.6 cents per gallon over the past month. ((-- New York Newsroom 212 859 1902))</p>
